From f6d8566952978e7d791c23908761d8f2e90e4f45 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jason McPheron <jason.mcpheron@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 00:29:08 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] fix: keep EIP-1271 contract signatures when rebuilding a
 queued tx (GS021)

createExistingTx (web) and addSignaturesToTx (mobile) added every confirmation from the
Transaction Service as a plain signature: staticPart = the whole stored signature, dynamicPart
= ''. A contract owner's confirmation (a nested Safe, a passkey signer) is stored as
{owner}{offset = 65}{00}{length}{data}, so it was concatenated whole with its offset still at 65.
With two or more signatures that offset points inside the static part and the Safe reverts with
GS021 in simulation and execution.

toSafeSignature (packages/utils) turns a stored confirmation back into an EthSafeSignature,
as a contract signature with just its data when v = 0, so buildSignatureBytes re-points it.
The test uses a real Base Sepolia transaction (a passkey owner and an EOA) and checks the
rebuilt bytes against the signatures the Safe executed.

Refs #3673
